Patch G3 (rung 2, task T0b): crate batch 3 in deny.toml's `[bans] allow`,
and the wrapper ban that keeps objc2-game-controller inside the GCMouse
shim. No `clarify` entry and no _typos.toml change: neither is needed
(notes below). This is the variant for the owner's recommended O3 answer,
the shim as a crate (after g2-gcmouse-crate.patch). The other two are
g3-crate-batch-3-shim-module.patch and g3-crate-batch-3-no-shim.patch.

Why: T14 adds objc2-game-controller to eng-platform-gcmouse (macOS only),
and T17 adds gungraun to eng-bench (a dev-dependency, Linux only).
cargo-deny fails on any crate outside `[bans] allow` for any target in
`[graph] targets`, whether or not that target builds it.

What (docs/rungs/2/plan.md, "Crate batch 3" and the G3 row of "Owner
gates"):
- `[bans] deny`: objc2-game-controller only as a direct dependency of
  eng-platform-gcmouse, the way wgpu and winit are kept inside eng-gpu and
  eng-platform-winit.
- `[bans] allow`: 17 names in a block after batch 2, sorted: the plan's
  15 and two it missed (difference 1). objc2-game-controller is written
  `objc2-game-controller:*`, as wgpu, winit and raw-window-handle are:
  cargo-deny 0.20.2 still refuses a bare name in both lists ("a crate was
  specified in both `allow` and `deny`", checked again with this crate).
- A comment on batch 3 after batch 2's.

Differences from the plan's list (proposed amendments to "Crate batch 3"):
1. Two more names: rustc_version 0.4.1 and semver 1.0.28, both MIT OR
   Apache-2.0. rustc_version is a build-dependency of derive_more-impl and
   gungraun-macros, and semver is a dependency of rustc_version. Both are
   in Cargo.lock already, but only through Android crates (jni-macros,
   simd_cesu8), which no target in `[graph]` reaches. So they are not in
   `allow` today, and cargo-deny refuses both without these entries. The
   plan probably counted them as allowed because the lock has them.
2. rustversion 1.0.23 is brought by rapidhash. For derive_more it is only
   a dev-dependency, outside our graph. The entry is the same.
Every version in the plan's table resolved as listed, with the licences it
gives.

Notes:
- arch-check fences objc2-game-controller too, in `quick`: the shim
  patch puts it in `[floor]` (`[E-ARCH-FLOOR]`). This ban is the same
  fence in CI's lint job.
- bincode-next's licence string, "MIT or Apache-2.0": cargo-deny 0.20.2
  reads it as MIT OR Apache-2.0 (`cargo deny list` in a scratch project
  where it is a normal dependency). Here it is not licence-checked at all:
  cargo-deny leaves dev-only crates out of the licence check (`include-dev`
  defaults to false), and the whole gungraun tree is dev-only. So it needs
  no `clarify` entry.
- typos (1.51.1) passes with the new names, so _typos.toml is unchanged.
- Until T14 depends on objc2-game-controller, its wrapper gives one more
  `unused-wrapper` warning, as gilrs and cpal do.
- No new duplicate-version warning: the 12 are today's.
- MSRVs: the highest is bincode-next's 1.90, below the pinned 1.99.1.

Base: main at c879061 with g2-crates.patch and g2-gcmouse-crate.patch
applied. At the repo root, run `git apply` with this file, then
`cargo xtask quick` and `cargo xtask ci --job lint`; quick runs neither
cargo-deny nor typos, the lint job runs both.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

How it was tested, on aarch64-apple-darwin with Rust 1.99.1, cargo-deny
0.20.2 and typos-cli 1.51.1, the advisory database fetched on 2026-11-07:
- Today's dependencies with this policy: `cargo deny check` exits 0.
- In a scratch copy with both G2 patches applied (not part of this patch),
  batch 3 added where the plan puts it: gungraun =0.20.0 under eng-bench's
  `[target.'cfg(target_os = "linux")'.dev-dependencies]`, and
  objc2-game-controller =0.3.2 (`default-features = false`; std, block2,
  GCDevice, GCMouse, GCMouseInput, GCPhysicalInputProfile) with objc2
  0.6.5 and block2 0.6.2 under the shim's
  `[target.'cfg(target_os = "macos")'.dependencies]`. Cargo.lock gained
  14 packages, all in the plan's table; the other three names were locked
  already. `cargo deny check` exits 0: advisories, bans, licenses and
  sources ok, with no warning beyond today's. With only the plan's 15
  names, bans fails on rustc_version and semver; without rustversion, on
  rustversion.
- objc2-game-controller added to eng-platform-winit, or to eng-app, as
  well: `cargo deny check bans` fails with `error[banned]`.
- `cargo check` of the shim with those features compiles on 1.99.1.
- This file applies with `git apply` to a fresh clone with both G2 patches
  applied, and gives the tested files byte for byte. There, `cargo xtask
  quick` and `CI=1 cargo xtask ci --job lint` are green.

